CORE libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11 --stdlib libc++
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ a write to stdout always succeeds: FAILURE$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 2 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
--
Fixed (soundness): the stream buffers of provide_standard_stream_objects
accepted every character, so a write never failed and assertion 1 was
reported to hold.  overflow may now return eof() and xsputn may write
any initial part of the characters.
